    improve (key/credit limit, Python harness only): an HTTP 403 'Key limit exceeded'/credit limit or a 402 (insufficient credits) pauses the model at once: operator hold (reason 'shared-balance priority', the provider text in the log), no retry loop. Tests: 'jevgammon ask' is watched; at the first answer of this asking that failed on the account limit it is stopped once none of its ledger reservations is open (in-flight requests settle first; after 5 s it is stopped anyway); failed positions stay stored and are re-asked when the hold is lifted. Games: a key-limit match failure or lesson call pauses (the series replays with the same dice on resume, the plan's rule); nothing is dispatched while held. Other 403s unchanged. Tests with a test double for ask (fake_ask.py): key limit mid-test, resume, ordinary 403, texts. Python 25 OK.

